.TH "waybar\-river\-tags" "5" "2026\-08\-08"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- river tags module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBtags\fR module displays the current state of tags in river.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBriver/tags\fR
.PP
\fBnum\-tags\fR: 
.br
typeof: uint 
.br
default: 9 
.br
The number of tags that should be displayed.\& Max 32.\&
.PP
\fBtag\-labels\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
The label to display for each tag.\&
.PP
\fBdisable\-click\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to false, you can left\-click to set focused tag.\& Right\-click to toggle tag focus.\& If set to true this behaviour is disabled.\&
.PP
\fBset\-tags\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
An array of tag bitmasks, one per tag button.\& Left\-clicking a tag sets the focused tags to the corresponding bitmask instead of the single tag.\& Requires \fBdisable\-click\fR to be false.\&
.PP
\fBtoggle\-tags\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
An array of tag bitmasks, one per tag button.\& Right\-clicking a tag toggles the corresponding bitmask in the focused tags instead of the single tag.\& Requires \fBdisable\-click\fR to be false.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables this module to consume all left over space dynamically.\&
.PP
\fBhide\-vacant\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Only show relevant tags: tags that are either focused or have a window on them.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"river/tags": {
	"num\-tags": 5
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sticky tag: this enables 5 tags and, to support a sticky tag (tag 32),
\fBset\-tags\fR is given bitmasks with the 32nd bit set so that tag stays selected
whichever button is clicked.\&
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"river/tags": {
	"num\-tags": 5,
	"set\-tags": [
		2147483649,
		2147483650,
		2147483652,
		2147483656,
		2147483664
	]
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#tags button\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#tags button.\&occupied\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#tags button.\&focused\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#tags button.\&urgent\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#tags button.\&output\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#tags button.\&tag\-N\fR
.PD
.PP
Note that occupied/focused/urgent/output status may overlap.\& That is, a tag may be
both occupied and focused at the same time.\&
.PP
The \fBoutput\fR style is applied when the river output (e.\&g.\& monitor) of the current bar is focused.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
